course: dictionary
lesson: 7785
title: Qin: a name, a family, a sound
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Qin is a name. In history it means the Qin dynasty, a family whose rule passed from parent to child. «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms and called himself Qin Shi Huang, the First Emperor.» Here Qin is the family and the state they ruled.
explain: Qin is not an ordinary English word, so you cannot guess it from its shape. Use the clues around it: «China was ruled by dynasties, such as the Shang, Zhou, Qin, Han, Tang, Song and Ming.» The list tells you Qin is one of those families of rulers.
explain: The same spelling can mean something different in another language. In Mandarin, pinyin «qín» names a stringed instrument, such as the guqin. The pinyin letter q sounds like English «ch», so Qin sounds like «chin».
fact: The Qin dynasty was short but very important: the state of Qin united the warring kingdoms of China in 221 BC.
fact: The first Qin emperor, Qin Shi Huang, made one system of writing, money and measures for the whole country.
fact: He was buried with the Terracotta Army, thousands of clay soldiers.
fact: In pinyin, «q» sounds like «ch», so Qin is said like «chin»; «qín» is a stringed instrument.
fact: Qin is also a Chinese family name, so it can belong to a person as well as to a dynasty.
exercise: «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms.» What is Qin in this sentence? | A type of paper | A kind of clay soldier | A stringed instrument | *A Chinese ruling family and its state
exercise: In Mandarin pinyin, the letter q is said like which English sound? | Qu, as in queen | *Ch, as in chin | Kw, as in quick | S, as in sun
exercise: Is Qin an ordinary English word? What kind of word is it? | A number | *A name, not an ordinary English word | A verb meaning to rule | A kind of paper
test: Which name belongs to the emperor who called himself First Emperor after uniting China under Qin? | *Qin Shi Huang | Shang | Tang | Zhang Qian
test: In Mandarin, what does «qín» most likely name? | A Chinese year | A kind of clay soldier | A city wall | *A stringed instrument, such as the guqin
exam: Which description fits the Qin dynasty best? | *A family of rulers who united China in 221 BC | A kind of Chinese paper | A word meaning very hungry | A stringed instrument played in lessons
